      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n\n    // Flatten matrix into a single vector for better spatial locality\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Integral image (summed-area table) with long long to avoid overflow\n    int stride = n + 1;\n    std::vector<long long> pref(stride * stride, 0);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[i * n + j];\n            pref[(i + 1) * stride + (j + 1)] =\n                pref[i * stride + (j + 1)] + row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Find maximum SxS submatrix sum using O(1) queries with 2D tiling\n    const int B = 64;\n    long long mxSum = -(1LL << 60);\n    for (int ib = 0; ib <= n - s; ib += B) {\n        int ie = std::min(n - s + 1, ib + B);\n        for (int jb = 0; jb <= n - s; jb += B) {\n            int je = std::min(n - s + 1, jb + B);\n            // Process tile [ib, ie) x [jb, je)\n            for (int i = ib; i < ie; ++i) {\n                const long long* row_i   = &pref[i * stride];\n                const long long* row_is  = &pref[(i + s) * stride];\n                for (int j = jb; j < je; ++j) {\n                    long long sum = row_is[j + s] - row_i[j + s] - row_is[j] + row_i[j];\n                    if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Apply 2D tiling on the query loops with block size B=64 to improve temporal reuse of integral image rows and columns in L1 cache. Within each tile, precompute row pointers (row_i and row_is) for fast indexed access without repeated stride multiplication.",
  "notes": "Tiling both i and j dimensions reduces cache misses by reusing loaded pref entries across neighboring queries. Block size 64 fits typical ARM L1 data cache line sizes and keeps working set small.",
